        "id": 8669,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-09-14T15:43:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This card from the Time Cataclysm Environment deck deals 1 damage to everything whenever a card is \"put into play\".&nbsp; I was not clear on whether this includes One-Shot cards, but we had Mr. Fixer in the game, and his Scrap Yard card says in part, \"Then, if you have the card Overdrive in your trash, you may <strong>put it into play</strong>.\"&nbsp; This somewhat odd wording seemed to imply that One-Shots do indeed trigger SST, so I went with that interpretation...and as a result, La Capitan ground through four already damage-dealing One-Shots in her turn, having gotten all of her other cards on the table by now, and we heroes died miserably when we'd already been losing by inches.</p><p>Did I play this correctly?&nbsp; Or is SST supposed to only be triggered by cards that stay in play past the resolution of their effects?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:15.162Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
